Modifications (2026-10 ~ 2026-11), listed per Apache-2.0 §4(b):

  added      memoryos/scoring.py, schema.py, audit.py, archive.py,
             consolidate.py, consolidate_llm.py
  changed    memoryos/mid_term.py, long_term.py, short_term.py,
             retriever.py, updater.py, memoryos.py, prompts.py
  added      run_consolidate.py, run_disposition.py
  added      docs/, tools/, tests/, README.md, NOTICE

What the modification does:

  * replaced heat-based eviction with a score/tier layer, then proved with real
    data that the layer does not work and disabled it
    (see docs/FORGETTING_BETA.md);
  * kept and hardened the data-safety base: no hard deletes, valid_to with
    --restore, atomic writes, corrupt-file quarantine, archive only on explicit
    human confirmation;
  * added a weekly human disposition sheet (run_disposition.py) that lists
    capacity-pressure and archive candidates and changes nothing.

The custom scoring layer is OFF by default: `USE_CUSTOM_SCORING` must be
explicitly set to 1/true/yes/on to enable it.

No personal data is included in this repository. Evaluation corpora and label
files are intentionally excluded; see data/README.md.